**/.git
**/.vs
**/.vscode
**/obj
**/bin
AsistOff.MES.Web
**/*.md
**/*.user
# Never bake local secrets into images — compose injects env at runtime
# (issue #308). Patterns cover the repo root and any nested copy, while the
# csproj-first COPY layering in the Dockerfile stays untouched.
.env
.env.local
.env.production
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.production
**/.env.*
# .NET user-secrets / ad-hoc secret files must never enter the context.
**/secrets.json
**/*.secrets.json
# Compose overrides carry host ports and secret references for local dev;
# the image never needs them (Coolify deploys with an explicit -f and
# ignores the override file).
docker-compose.override.yml
docker-compose.swarm.yml
compose.override.yml
# Issue #364: keep the Development settings (dev seed defaults) out of the
# build context so no shipped layer can contain a seed credential. The Gateway
# csproj additionally sets CopyToPublishDirectory=Never for the same file, so
# dotnet publish omits it from the runtime image; local dev still reads it
# from the source tree.
**/appsettings.Development.json
